<title>USA: Hills closes two Kentucky stores; 149 lose jobs.</title>
<headline>Hills closes two Kentucky stores; 149 lose jobs.</headline>
<dateline>CANTON, Mass. 1997-02-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hills Stores Co told workers Saturday it would close two Lexington, Ky stores during the first quarter of 1997.</p>
<p>The closings are in addition to an earlier announcement in which the Canton, Massachusetts-based discount retailer said it would close eight stores.</p>
<p>A total of 149 workers will be affected by the April shutdown of the two stores, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>After the closings in Kentucky, North Carolina, Ohio and Virginia, Hills will operate 155 stores, the company said.</p>
<p>--Boston bureau, 617-367-4106)</p>
</text>
